{"name":"Jungle Expedition","hex":"#b49356","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"jungle","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A large, lush, undeveloped, humid forest, especially in a tropical region, thick with vegetation and wildlife; a tropical  rainforest.","Any uncultivated tract of forest or scrub habitat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["(Of musical beat, rhythm, etc.) resembling the fast-paced drumming of traditional peoples of the jungle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jungle"},{"term":"expedition","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A military journey; an enterprise against some enemy or into enemy territory.","An important or long journey, for example a march or a voyage."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To take part in a trip or expedition; to travel."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/expedition"}],"entries":[{"title":"Jungle","blocks":[{"text":"A jungle is an area of land covered with dense forest and tangled vegetation, usually in tropical climates. Application of the term has varied greatly during the past century. Because jungles occur on all inhabited landmasses and may incorporate numerous vegetation and land types in different climatic zones, the wildlife of jungles cannot be straightforwardly defined."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg/330px-%E1%9E%96%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%9A%E1%9F%83%E1%9E%80%E1%9E%98%E1%9F%92%E1%9E%96%E1%9E%BB%E1%9E%87%E1%9E%B6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jungle","wikidata":"Q191086"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Tioman_Rainforest.JPG/500px-Tioman_Rainforest.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/